Keeps which strand does what, and how the strand system itself should work.

The meta-strand — custodian of the strand *model*: the map of which strand does what, and the theory behind it (the strand pattern, what STATE/IDEAS/CLAUDE.md are for, the emerging distinctions — keeper vs development strands, STATE-stickiness, the metrics principle, blurb format, session ritual). It decides *what* the system should do; the practical half that *builds* it — `aicli`, the `.template` scaffolds, `idea`/`ding`, the manywrapper — lives in [[aifabric]] ("aifabric is practical stranding, strands is strand theory"). Curation output lands in `strands/README.md`, the templates' shape, and `super/GLOBAL.md` conventions.
